.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/briefs/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.log
# Machine-local session rules. Describes one box, not the project.
CLAUDE.local.md

# OLMA recording (230 MB) and its extracted frames stay local. Aurik pulls this repo.
notes/olma/*.mp4
notes/olma/frames/

# Catalogue downloads and the database built from them: 9.1 GB, one file of it 7.4 GB.
# Every byte is re-fetchable from Open Food Facts and Canada's open data by the
# scripts in catalogue/src. Nothing here is authored.
catalogue/data/

# Crawled shelf prices and the SQLite files SQLite writes beside them. Every row is
# re-fetchable by price/src/crawl.ts from the retailer it names, and a price a week old
# is worse than no price. Nothing here is authored.
price/data/
# NOTE, because one file in there is not like the others: prices.db is ignored
# because a re-crawl rebuilds it. corrections.db cannot be rebuilt by anything.
# It is one person's eyes on one shelf on one day. It stays out of git (a binary
# holding other people's contributions does not belong in a repo a collaborator
# clones), which means that until this runs on a real server it exists on
# exactly one machine with no backup.

# Camera bundle and the WebAssembly it needs: build output of
# `node app/scripts/build-eye.mjs`, 35 MB, pinned by app/package-lock.json.
app/public/js/eye.js
app/public/js/eye.js.map
app/public/js/chunks/
app/public/js/vendor/

# Local SQLite runtime state (plus its -shm/-wal lock files). Rebuilt by the app.
app/data/
# identify/data/ is runtime state like the three above: spend-cap.json (the daily
# dollar cap's store, identify/src/cap.ts) and a gaps.db that the eval runner leaves
# behind when run from that directory. Nothing in it is tracked and nothing in it can
# be rebuilt from git, which is the same reason app/data/ is here. Added 2026-09-14
# after a gaps.db showed up untracked and un-ignored in a lane's git status.
identify/data/

# A ROOT-LEVEL data/, which is a different thing from the four above: it is
# written when a tool that expects to run inside its own package is run from
# the repo root instead (data/gaps.db, 2026-09-14). Ignored rather than
# deleted, because the tool is the thing to fix and a stray database is not
# worth losing; ignored rather than left loose, because the next blanket
# `git add` would otherwise pick it up, which is the failure the no-blind-add
# hook exists to prevent and this line makes impossible.
/data/

# Eval output. A run's numbers belong in NOW.md and in a commit message where
# somebody reads them, not as a JSON file that quietly accumulates one per run.
identify/eval/results/

# The Mac beta server's own settings, filled in from mac/config.env.example. It
# holds the Cloudflare tunnel connector token and the beta invite code, so it is
# a credential file and not a config file, whatever its extension says. The
# .env rules above do not catch it: they match a file named .env, and this one
# is named config.env.
mac/config.env
